# Kleeblatt Adventure — Phaser/React Audit Notes

## 1. Fixed: `phaser3spectorjs` module resolution error

**Error:**
```
Uncaught TypeError: Failed to resolve module specifier "phaser3spectorjs"
```

**Cause:** `apps/web/vite.config.ts` had:
```ts
resolve: {
  alias: {
    phaser: resolve(__dirname, "../../node_modules/phaser/src/phaser.js"),
  },
},
```
This aliased Phaser to its raw, uncompiled source tree instead of its published entry point. Deep inside that tree, `WebGLRenderer.js` has a bare `import` of `phaser3spectorjs` — an optional dev-only dependency never meant to be resolved by consumers. Vite couldn't resolve it, so the literal specifier shipped to the browser, which can't resolve bare specifiers at runtime.

**Fix applied:** removed the alias entirely. Confirmed working — the `phaser3spectorjs` error is gone and the game now reaches boot (Phaser v4.2.1 banner logs, `ready` event fires).

