## 3. Current/next crash to chase — inside Phaser's own code via `anims.create`

**Error (from your screenshot):**
```
ReferenceError: Phaser is not defined
  at new IO (...)
  at tm.create (...)
  at initialize.create (bootScene)
  at initialize.start
```

This is thrown *inside Phaser's library internals*, triggered from `this.anims.create(...)` in `boot-scene.ts` — not from a missing import in your own code (boot-scene.ts imports Phaser correctly).

**Best current lead (not yet verified against a real build):** Phaser 4's official Vite template (`npm create @phaserjs/game`) deliberately splits Phaser into its own build chunk — documented as a Phaser-4-specific requirement, different from the Phaser 3 templates. Worth trying:

```ts
// vite.config.ts
export default defineConfig({
  plugins: [react()],
  build: {
    rollupOptions: {
      output: { manualChunks: { phaser: ["phaser"] } },
    },
  },
  server: {
    port: 5173,
    proxy: {
      "/api": { target: "http://localhost:4000", changeOrigin: true },
      "/health": { target: "http://localhost:4000", changeOrigin: true },
      "/auth": { target: "http://localhost:4000", changeOrigin: true },
      "/me": { target: "http://localhost:4000", changeOrigin: true },
    },
  },
});
```

**Confidence:** medium. I couldn't run your actual build (no network/node_modules in my sandbox) to confirm this resolves the exact crash — treat it as the next thing to try, then report back what the console shows.

