## 4. Earlier finding — Phaser game recreated on every parent re-render

In `MatchPage.tsx`, the effect that creates/destroys the Phaser game depended on `onMatchResult`, which was a new function every render because `useHero()` (in `HomePage.tsx`) returns a fresh `{ state, refresh }` object on every render. Net effect: the running Phaser game tears down and rebuilds on ordinary React re-renders — most visibly right after a match ends.

**Fix (recommended, not yet confirmed applied):** hold `onMatchResult` in a `ref` and make the game-creation effect run once on mount/unmount only:

```ts
const onMatchResultRef = useRef(onMatchResult);
useEffect(() => { onMatchResultRef.current = onMatchResult; }, [onMatchResult]);

useEffect(() => {
  const container = containerRef.current;
  if (!container) return;
  const game = createGame(container);
  // ...
  const onEnded = (payload) => {
    // ...
    onMatchResultRef.current?.({ ... });
  };
  gameBridge.on("match:ended", onEnded);
  return () => { gameBridge.off("match:ended", onEnded); game.destroy(true); };
}, []); // mount/unmount only
```

Same churn pattern applies to the `handleStart` effect right below it in `MatchPage.tsx`.

